course: dictionary
lesson: 4890
title: A shameful fall
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Ignominiously is a long word, but its clues are in the sentence around it. Read «The Rat lists what Toad has been: handcuffed, imprisoned, starved, chased, terrified out of your life, insulted, jeered at, and ignominiously flung into the water—by a woman, too!» Toad is being thrown into the water, and the words insulted and jeered at tell you that people are laughing at him. So ignominiously means shamefully.
explain: The word is about how something happens, so it is an adverb. It tells you how Toad was flung into the water: in a way that made him feel small and embarrassed in front of others. In The Wind in the Willows, Toad is often a boaster, so his falls hurt his pride even more.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Swap in shamefully: «...and shamefully flung into the water» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. If a sentence says a team was «ignominiously knocked out by a small club», it means the team lost in a way that made them look foolish.
fact: Ignominiously means in a way that causes great shame or embarrassment in front of others.
fact: Ignominiously is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens.
fact: Ignominiously is close in meaning to shamefully and humiliatingly.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad is often ignominiously dumped, falling into the mud or being thrown into the river.
fact: Context clues such as insulted and jeered at can show you that a word is about shame.
exercise: «The team were ignominiously knocked out by a small club.» What does ignominiously mean here? | *In a way that brings great shame and embarrassment | Late, after the match had ended | Very quickly and quietly | Happily, with a big cheer from the crowd
exercise: The Rat says Toad was flung into the water «ignominiously». Why is the fall ignominious, and not just a fall? | The water was cold | *It was embarrassing, in front of others, and made Toad feel small | It was night time | Toad was asleep when it happened
exercise: «The team were ignominiously knocked out by a small club.» Find and copy the word that tells how the team were knocked out. | knocked | team | *ignominiously | were
test: Ignominiously means the same as which word? | Slowly | Happily | *Shamefully | Quietly
test: Which sentence uses ignominiously correctly? | She ignominiously won the spelling prize and cheered | *The proud captain was ignominiously beaten by the youngest player, in front of the whole school | He ignominiously ate his lunch at the picnic | The dog ignominiously barked at the postman all morning
exam: Toad boasts that he is the best driver, then falls in the mud in front of all his friends. Which word best describes how he falls? | Happily | Gently | *Ignominiously | Secretly
